Archally Brandvoice Schema - Licensing Overview
===============================================

Copyright 2026 Adam Walkowski

This repository is distributed under TWO licenses. Which one applies depends on
which part of the repository you are using. This file is the authoritative map;
the full legal texts are in the referenced files.


1. The open format - Apache License, Version 2.0
------------------------------------------------

The following are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(full text: ./LICENSE-APACHE, SPDX: Apache-2.0):

  - schema/                        the Brandvoice schema itself (the format definition)
  - examples/                      example brandvoice models
  - docs/                          the documentation
  - tools/schema-atlas/            schema reference generated from the format
  - tools/doc-snippet-validate/    conformance of documented model examples
  - tools/validator/               the reference conformance validator
  - tools/port/                    verifies the shipped files against the manifest
                                   published with them; it describes no brand and
                                   reads no model

The format is meant to be adopted freely. You may use, modify, and redistribute
these parts - including in commercial and proprietary products - under the terms
of the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Conformance is the reason the validator sits here rather than below. A format
whose only complete definition is a tool you cannot freely run is not an open
format, so the thing that answers "is this model valid?" carries the same license
as the schema it answers for. The same reasoning puts the port verifier here: it
is what a RECIPIENT runs to confirm they received what was published.

Where the line falls, for a tool added later: Apache-2.0 covers the format and
what is needed to establish conformance with it, plus the integrity of this
distribution. FSL covers everything that reads a model for a purpose other than
validating it - building its graph, naming what its edges mean, judging whether
it says enough, turning it into documents. Those are positions about what a good
model is, not properties of the format.


2. The tooling - Functional Source License 1.1 (ALv2 Future License)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The following are licensed under the Functional Source License, Version 1.1,
with an Apache 2.0 future grant (full text: ./LICENSE-FSL, SPDX: FSL-1.1-ALv2):

  - tools/entity-query/            inspect and filter a built model
  - tools/next-id/                 suggest entity identifiers in a model
  - tools/model-builder/           the model graph, and the relation vocabulary that
                                   says what each edge means
  - tools/semantic-checker/        model-quality rules and the adapter that feeds them

You may use, modify, and redistribute this code for any Permitted Purpose -
which includes internal use, non-commercial education and research, and
professional services you provide to others using the Software. You may NOT use
it for a Competing Use: making it available to others in a commercial product or
service that substitutes for, or offers substantially similar functionality to,
the Software or any product or service Archally offers using it.

Each version becomes available under the Apache License, Version 2.0 on the
SECOND ANNIVERSARY of the date that version was first made available. See
LICENSE-FSL for the exact terms.

The line between the two sections is the line between conformance and judgment.
Whether a model is VALID is a property of the format, and must be freely
checkable by anyone. Whether a model is GOOD - whether it says enough to be
worth having - is a set of opinions about modeling, and those are the product.


3. Dependencies
---------------

The rule engine the semantic checker runs on is a separate package,
@archally/semantic-checker, licensed Apache-2.0 under its own terms. Only the
brandvoice rules and the adapter feeding them are covered by section 2.


Scope note
----------

Neither license extends to:

  (a) brands, products, or communication strategies that are described by these
      schemas - your model of your own brand is yours; or

  (b) software that reads or writes brandvoice models without incorporating the
      parts listed above.
